      "Compact controls measure their rendered content after the safe first frame. The Browser fixture converges to a 500px panel around 498px of content; exact Native converges to 504px around 502px of content.",
      "The compact menu's last Full access row is now visible in Browser and exact Native, the panel and checkout context remain before the right-panel boundary, and fullscreen outside dismissal succeeds."
    ],
    "harnessMismatch": [
      "The narrow file-detail workbench reaches matching 359px editors, no explorers, matching 28px Back actions, real dual-client Back recovery, and zero console errors, but its aggregate reachedTargetState bookkeeping still reports false after the detail-to-browser transition. The frame is retained as strict diagnostic evidence, not admitted as a canonical matrix pass.",
      "The earlier compact menu harness omitted last-row visibility and counted hidden DOM rows as success. Browser and Native verifiers now require the final Full access row to end inside the scroll viewport.",
      "Early compact controls evidence used estimated panel height only. Dynamic provider row sets exposed both a clipped 476px Browser fixture and a 528px Native empty tail; only the final rendered-content measurements receive current credit."
    ],
    "remainingProductResidual": [
